NAME

ping - Send ICMP echo requests

SYNOPSIS

    ping [OPTIONS] HOST
    ping [-c|--count COUNT] [-i|--interval SECONDS] HOST

DESCRIPTION

Send ICMP echo requests.

OPTIONS

    -c COUNT, --count COUNT — Send a selected number of requests (1-1000).
    -i SECONDS, --interval SECONDS — Default 1 second; minimum 0.002 seconds.
    -h, --help — Show this help.

NOTES

Use -- before a hostname beginning with a hyphen. Fractional intervals round up to a millisecond; with this single-request API, a shorter interval also bounds the echo timeout.

